# NasSimHub UFI003 stick: USB NCM link to the NAS.
#
# The stick's gadget identifies itself as idVendor 1d6b / idProduct 0104 with
# manufacturer "NasSimHub" (overlay/usr/local/libexec/nassimhub-usb on the
# stick). Only that interface is touched: the QDC507 modem on this NAS is also
# a USB network device and must keep its own configuration.
#
# NetworkManager is told to leave the interface alone, otherwise it would run
# DHCP on it (the stick deliberately runs no DHCP server) and flush the static
# address set below.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="net", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1d6b", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0104", ATTRS{manufacturer}=="NasSimHub", ENV{NM_UNMANAGED}="1"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1d6b", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0104", ATTRS{manufacturer}=="NasSimHub", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="nassimhub-usb-link@$name.service"
